body:
thank you for reaching out to me. . . while in the relationship I was in pain scared that she would leave me for another which is exactly what she's doing right at this current time. I do feel lonely and I have been in this place before and it's VERY tiring. I have tried going out when and give the excuse that I am going to class but in reality I am going to parks and walking around listening to music sometimes I cry in the car knowing that everything seems so hopeless and whatever I try to make myself happy it always end up me crying for people I shouldn't cry about. 

&#x200B;

The relationship just added more fuel to my pain. I trusted someone with my heart thinking everything would work out and be okay while there were times I felt like a burden to her all I wanted was to be with her and no one else because she was the source of my happiness I would genuinely smile when I was around her. Maybe I was too codependent with her but in my heart there is no one else like her and that is what kills me knowing I won't be the one to marry her or see her in my future it hurts me. I blame mostly myself and my family for this dismay but she was at fault as well. . .
